      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Machine Learning for Intelligent Vehicles\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "**IGNITE Batavia Team × Universitas Negeri Jakarta**\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.7em; color: #aaa; margin-top: 60px;\">\n",
        "Today is not about becoming ML experts — it's about direct, first-hand experience with ML workflows.\n",
        "</div>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Why Are Vehicles Becoming Intelligent? {background-color=\"#1a1a2e\"}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.incremental}\n",
        "- **Roads are dynamic** — unpredictable environment\n",
        "- **Energy is limited** — battery must be managed\n",
        "- **Safety decisions are fast** — milliseconds matter\n",
        "- **Sensors generate huge data** — too much for manual rules\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    S[Sensors] --> D[Data Stream]\n",
        "    D --> M[ML Models]\n",
        "    M --> A[Action]\n",
        "    A -->|feedback| S\n",
        "\n",
        "    style S fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style M fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style A fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.7em; color: #888; margin-top: 20px;\">\n",
        "Intelligence is not a luxury feature — it's a practical engineering need.\n",
        "</div>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Workshop Journey {background-color=\"#1a1a2e\"}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\" style=\"text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "### Inside the Vehicle\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "⚡ **Battery Sensors** → 📊 **SoC Estimation**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #aaa;\">\n",
        "Current, Voltage, Temperature → State of Charge\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\" style=\"text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "### Outside the Vehicle\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "📷 **Camera Image** → 🎯 **Object Detection**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #aaa;\">\n",
        "Pixels → Cars, People, Traffic Lights\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "Two different data types — one unified ML workflow.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# What Will You Build Today? {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    A[📥 Load Data] --> B[🔧 Prepare Features]\n",
        "    B --> C[🤖 Train Model]\n",
        "    C --> D[📈 Evaluate]\n",
        "    D --> E[🔮 Predict]\n",
        "    E --> F[🧠 Interpret]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style A fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style C fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style E fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "    style F fill:#9b51e0,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "### Part 1: Battery SoC\n",
        "Train models to estimate battery charge from sensor readings\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "### Part 2: Object Detection\n",
        "Use pretrained YOLOv8 to detect road objects from camera images\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# What Is Machine Learning? {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "### Traditional Programming\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    R[Rules] --> P{Program}\n",
        "    D[Data] --> P\n",
        "    P --> A[Answer]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style R fill:#eb5757,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.85em; color: #777;\">\n",
        "You write the logic\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"10%\" style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 2em; padding-top: 60px;\"}\n",
        "**→**\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "### Machine Learning\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    D[Data] --> M{Model}\n",
        "    A[Answer Examples] --> M\n",
        "    M --> P[Learned Pattern]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style M fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style P fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.85em; color: #777;\">\n",
        "The model learns patterns from examples\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip icon=false}\n",
        "Instead of writing every battery rule manually, show the model many examples of \"sensor readings → known SoC\" and let it learn.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# ML in an Intelligent Vehicle {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Examples of ML Tasks\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "- 📊 **Estimate battery charge** → from voltage & current\n",
        "- 🚗 **Detect cars and pedestrians** → from camera feed\n",
        "- ⚠️ **Predict maintenance risk** → from usage patterns\n",
        "- 🛑 **Decide when to slow down** → from detected obstacles\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "ML is one component inside a larger system — it feeds predictions to the controller, not directly to the brakes.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    subgraph Perception[\"👁️ Perception\"]\n",
        "        B[SoC Estimation]\n",
        "        C[Object Detection]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "    subgraph Planning[\"🧠 Planning\"]\n",
        "        D[Energy Strategy]\n",
        "        E[Driving Decision]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "    subgraph Control[\"🎮 Control\"]\n",
        "        F[Throttle/Brake]\n",
        "        G[Battery Management]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "\n",
        "    B --> D\n",
        "    C --> E\n",
        "    D --> G\n",
        "    E --> F\n",
        "\n",
        "    style Perception fill:#1a1a2e,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Planning fill:#2d3436,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Control fill:#1a1a2e,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# The Four Words We Need {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "| Word | Simple Meaning | Vehicle Example |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---|\n",
        "| **Feature** | Input data the model reads | Current, Voltage, Temperature |\n",
        "| **Target** | What we want to predict | State of Charge (0 to 100%) |\n",
        "| **Training** | Learning from examples | Fresh battery data with known SoC |\n",
        "| **Prediction** | Model's output on new data | Estimated SoC from new sensors |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip icon=false}\n",
        "Four words. That's enough vocabulary to follow today's entire workflow.  \n",
        "Everything else is detail.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Supervised Learning Intuition {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "### Training Phase\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Current (A) | Voltage (V) | Temp (°C) | **SoC?** |\n",
        "|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n",
        "| 2.36 | 2.99 | 27.4 | **100%** |\n",
        "| -19.8 | 3.75 | 26.1 | **56%** |\n",
        "| 20.1 | 3.92 | 26.8 | **78%** |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.85em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Model sees: sensors + known answer → learns the mapping\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"4%\" style=\"font-size: 2em; padding-top: 80px; text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "→\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "### Prediction Phase\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Current (A) | Voltage (V) | Temp (°C) | **SoC?** |\n",
        "|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n",
        "| -4.3 | 3.68 | 26.5 | **??** |\n",
        "| 15.7 | 4.05 | 27.1 | **??** |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.85em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Model sees: sensors only → estimates the answer\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note icon=false}\n",
        "Like studying with answer keys, then taking the exam.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# ML Workflow in One Diagram {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    A[🗂️ Raw Data\\nTime, Current, Voltage, Temp] --> B[⚙️ Feature Engineering\\ncum_charge, OCV-SOC mapping]\n",
        "    B --> C[📊 Train / Test Split\\nFresh cell → train\\nAged cell → test]\n",
        "    C --> D[🤖 Model Training\\nRandom Forest / XGBoost]\n",
        "    D --> E[📈 Evaluation\\nMAE, RMSE, R²]\n",
        "    E --> F[🧠 Explainability\\nSHAP feature importance]\n",
        "    F --> G[🔮 Predict on New Data]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style A fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style D fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style G fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "This exact flow is what you'll see in the notebook. The presentation explains the **why** — the notebook handles the **how**.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Part 1: Battery State of Charge {background-color=\"#1a1a2e\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "**Can a vehicle estimate battery SoC from sensor data?**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    S[⚡ Sensors] --> M[🤖 ML Model] --> G[📊 SoC Gauge]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style S fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style M fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style G fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "SoC is like a fuel gauge — but batteries behave non-linearly depending on current, voltage, temperature, and age.\n",
        "</div>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Why SoC Estimation Matters {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### If SoC is Wrong\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "- ❌ Vehicle may **overestimate range** → stranded\n",
        "- ❌ **Inefficient charging** → wasted energy\n",
        "- ❌ **Battery degradation** → shorter lifespan\n",
        "- ❌ **Poor energy decisions** → safety risk\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "A 5% SoC error on a 300 km range = 15 km of uncertainty.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    SOC[Accurate SoC] --> R[✅ Reliable Range]\n",
        "    SOC --> E[✅ Efficient Charging]\n",
        "    SOC --> S[✅ Battery Safety]\n",
        "    SOC --> M[✅ Smart Energy Mgmt]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style SOC fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Our Sensor Data {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### What the Battery Management System Records\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Column | Unit | Meaning | Example Range |\n",
        "|:---|:---:|:---|:---|\n",
        "| **Time** | `s` | Elapsed time | 0 → 307,513 (~85 hours) |\n",
        "| **Current** | `A` | Charging (+) / Discharging (−) | −20 to +33 |\n",
        "| **Voltage** | `V` | Terminal voltage | 3.0 → 4.2 |\n",
        "| **Temperature** | `°C` | Cell temperature | 25 → 28 |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note icon=false}\n",
        "**Two datasets:** Fresh battery (358K rows) → **training.** Aged battery (307K rows) → **testing.**  \n",
        "Plus an OCV-SOC lookup table (1001 points) for calibration.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Coulomb Counting — The Physics Behind SoC {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### How We Create the Ground Truth Label\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;\">\n",
        "$$SOC(t) = SOC(0) - \\frac{1}{C_{nom}} \\int_{0}^{t} I(\\tau) \\, d\\tau$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### In Plain Terms\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Measure current every second\n",
        "2. Multiply current × time → charge (Ah)\n",
        "3. Subtract from full capacity\n",
        "4. Calibrate with OCV when current ≈ 0\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.85em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Notebook function: `compute_soc()` and `compute_capacity()`\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    A[Current × ΔTime] --> B[Δ Charge]\n",
        "    B --> C[Accumulate over time]\n",
        "    C --> D[Divide by Capacity]\n",
        "    D --> E[Subtract from 100%]\n",
        "    F[OCV Voltage] -.->|calibrate when idle| E\n",
        "    E --> G[SOC_true Target]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style G fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Feature Engineering {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### From Raw Sensors to ML-Ready Data\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Feature | Source | Why It Helps |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---|\n",
        "| **Current** | Raw sensor | Charging/discharging direction and rate |\n",
        "| **Voltage** | Raw sensor | Strong correlation with SoC via OCV curve |\n",
        "| **Temperature** | Raw sensor | Affects battery behavior |\n",
        "| **cum_charge** | Engineered | Cumulative charge — model sees history, not just instant |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "The `cum_charge` feature is **not** in the raw data. It's computed by integrating current over time — giving the model a sense of \"how much energy has flowed.\"\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Notebook: build_features() creates the feature matrix from the raw DataFrame.\n",
        "</div>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Train / Test Split Strategy {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\" style=\"text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "### Training Data\n",
        "🪫 **Fresh Battery Cell**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "- 358K rows\n",
        "- Brand new behavior\n",
        "- Model learns the \"ideal\" mapping\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "\"Here are many examples of new battery behavior. Learn this.\"\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"4%\" style=\"font-size: 2em; padding-top: 80px; text-align: center;\"}>\n",
        "→\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\" style=\"text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "### Test Data\n",
        "🔋 **Aged Battery Cell**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "- 307K rows\n",
        "- Degraded behavior\n",
        "- Does the model generalize?\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "\"If the model only saw fresh batteries, can it still estimate an aged one?\"\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "A model trained on one condition may fail on another. **This is why testing matters.**\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Model 1: Random Forest {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "### Intuition\n",
        "\n",
        "Many decision trees vote together.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each tree sees a random subset of data and features.\n",
        "\n",
        "The average of all trees → final prediction.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    D[Input Features] --> T1[Tree 1]\n",
        "    D --> T2[Tree 2]\n",
        "    D --> T3[...]\n",
        "    D --> T4[Tree N]\n",
        "    T1 --> V[Majority Vote]\n",
        "    T2 --> V\n",
        "    T3 --> V\n",
        "    T4 --> V\n",
        "    V --> P[SoC Prediction]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style D fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style V fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style P fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "### Why It Works for SoC\n",
        "\n",
        "- Handles **nonlinear** Voltage-SoC relationship\n",
        "- Robust to noisy sensor readings\n",
        "- Easy to interpret with feature importance\n",
        "- Good baseline for tabular data\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "### In the Notebook\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "# Simplified — your notebook has the full version\n",
        "rf = RandomForestRegressor(\n",
        "    n_estimators=100,\n",
        "    max_depth=15,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "rf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Training time: ~2 minutes on the full dataset\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Model 2: XGBoost {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "### Intuition\n",
        "\n",
        "Unlike Random Forest (parallel trees), XGBoost builds trees **sequentially**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each new tree tries to **fix the mistakes** of the previous trees.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    M1[Model 1] -->|errors| M2[Model 2]\n",
        "    M2 -->|errors| M3[Model 3]\n",
        "    M3 -->|errors| MN[...]\n",
        "    MN -->|sum| P[Final Prediction]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style M1 fill:#eb5757,color:#fff\n",
        "    style M2 fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style M3 fill:#f2c94c,color:#000\n",
        "    style P fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "### Why It's Stronger\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Gradient boosting** — each step reduces error\n",
        "- Often beats Random Forest on tabular data\n",
        "- Built-in regularization prevents overfitting\n",
        "- Industry favorite for competitions\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "### In the Notebook\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "xgb = XGBRegressor(\n",
        "    n_estimators=300,\n",
        "    max_depth=10,\n",
        "    learning_rate=0.05\n",
        ")\n",
        "xgb.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Training time: ~10 seconds — much faster than RF!\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# RF vs XGBoost — Side by Side {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Aspect | Random Forest | XGBoost |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---|\n",
        "| **How trees build** | Parallel (independent) | Sequential (each fixes previous) |\n",
        "| **Training speed** | Slower (~2 min) | Faster (~10 sec) |\n",
        "| **Overfitting risk** | Low (built-in averaging) | Moderate (needs tuning) |\n",
        "| **Accuracy (R²)** | 0.423 | 0.496 |\n",
        "| **Best for** | Quick baselines, interpretation | When you need the extra accuracy |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "Neither model is perfect. R² ≈ 0.5 means there's **room for improvement** — a good discussion point: what other features could help?\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# How to Read the Results {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### Three Metrics — What They Actually Mean\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Metric | Meaning | Good SoC Value | The Question It Answers |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---:|:---|\n",
        "| **MAE** | Average absolute error | < 0.05 | \"On average, how far off am I in SoC units?\" |\n",
        "| **RMSE** | Penalizes large errors | < 0.10 | \"How bad are the worst predictions?\" |\n",
        "| **R²** | Variance explained (0-1) | > 0.8 | \"What fraction of SoC variation did the model capture?\" |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "**MAE = 0.10 means:** on average, the model is off by 10% SoC.  \n",
        "For a vehicle with 300 km range, that's **30 km of uncertainty** — worth improving!\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Model Interpretation with SHAP {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### Asking the Model: \"What Were You Looking At?\"\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### SHAP Values\n",
        "\n",
        "SHAP tells us which features **pushed** each prediction up or down.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each prediction gets an explanation:\n",
        "- **Red** = feature pushed prediction higher\n",
        "- **Blue** = feature pushed prediction lower\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.85em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Notebook uses `shap.TreeExplainer()` + `summary_plot()`\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Why This Matters for Engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "- ✅ **Debugging** — Is the model ignoring an important sensor?\n",
        "- ✅ **Trust** — Does it rely on physics (voltage) or noise?\n",
        "- ✅ **Regulation** — Can we explain decisions?\n",
        "- ✅ **Feature selection** — Which sensors can we remove?\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "In safety-critical systems, **knowing why** is as important as knowing the output.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Part 2: Object Detection {background-color=\"#1a1a2e\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "### From Sensor Tables to Road Cameras\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\" style=\"text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "### Inside\n",
        "📊 **Numbers in a Table**\n",
        "\n",
        "Current, Voltage, Temp → SoC\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"10%\" style=\"font-size: 2em; padding-top: 40px; text-align: center;\"}>\n",
        "→\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\" style=\"text-align: center;\"}\n",
        "### Outside\n",
        "🖼️ **Pixels in an Image**\n",
        "\n",
        "Camera feed → Objects in the scene\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note icon=false}\n",
        "Same ML principle. Different data structure.  \n",
        "Tabular ML reads columns. Computer vision reads spatial patterns.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Why Computer Vision for Vehicles? {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "### Before a Vehicle Can Decide...\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "It must **perceive** what is around it:\n",
        "\n",
        "- 🚶 **People** — pedestrians, cyclists\n",
        "- 🚗 **Vehicles** — cars, motorcycles, buses, trucks\n",
        "- 🚦 **Traffic elements** — lights, signs, lanes\n",
        "- 🛑 **Obstacles** — barriers, debris\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.85em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "Perception is the first step. Without it, no intelligent decision is possible.\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    C[📷 Camera] --> D[Object Detection]\n",
        "    D --> F[🚶 Person at 15m]\n",
        "    D --> G[🚗 Car at 30m]\n",
        "    D --> H[🚦 Traffic Light ahead]\n",
        "    F --> P[🧠 Planning Module]\n",
        "    G --> P\n",
        "    H --> P\n",
        "    P --> A[Decision: Slow down, maintain distance]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style C fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style P fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style A fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Three Computer Vision Tasks {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Task | Question | Output |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---|\n",
        "| **Classification** | \"What is in the image?\" | Single label: \"car\" |\n",
        "| **Object Detection** | \"What and where?\" | Boxes + labels + confidence |\n",
        "| **Segmentation** | \"Which pixel belongs to what?\" | Pixel-level masks |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    I[Input Image] --> C[Classification\\n\"Car\"]\n",
        "    I --> D[Detection\\n\"Car\" at x,y,w,h]\n",
        "    I --> S[Segmentation\\nEvery pixel labeled]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style C fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style D fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "    style S fill:#9b51e0,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "Today's focus: **Object Detection** — because vehicles need to know what objects exist AND where they are.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Object Detection Output Explained {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### For Each Detected Object\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Field | Example | Meaning |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---|\n",
        "| **Class name** | `\"car\"` | What the object is |\n",
        "| **Bounding box** | `(x1: 100, y1: 200, x2: 300, y2: 400)` | Where it is in the image |\n",
        "| **Confidence** | `0.85` | How sure the model is (0 to 1) |\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "**Confidence ≠ accuracy.** A high confidence (0.95) doesn't guarantee the detection is correct — it just means the model is internally confident. Always inspect results.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Meet YOLOv8 {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Y**ou **O**nly **L**ook **O**nce\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "### Why YOLO?\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Single pass** — one forward pass predicts all objects\n",
        "- **Real-time** — fast enough for video\n",
        "- **Pretrained** — works out of the box on 80 COCO classes\n",
        "- **YOLOv8n** — nano version, ideal for workshops\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "Today: **inference only.** We use a pretrained model.  \n",
        "Training from scratch takes days on server GPUs.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    I[📷 Image] --> Y[YOLO Model]\n",
        "    Y --> O[Detected Objects]\n",
        "    O --> B[Boxes + Classes + Scores]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style I fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Y fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style O fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "| Variant | Size | Speed | Use Case |\n",
        "|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n",
        "| YOLOv8n | Nano | Fastest | Edge devices, demos |\n",
        "| YOLOv8s | Small | Fast | Lightweight apps |\n",
        "| YOLOv8m | Medium | Balanced | General purpose |\n",
        "| YOLOv8x | X-Large | Slowest | Max accuracy |\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Why Pretrained Models? {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "### The Trade-Off\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "**✅ Advantages**\n",
        "- Ready to use immediately\n",
        "- Trained on millions of images\n",
        "- Good for demos and prototypes\n",
        "- No GPU training needed\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "**⚠️ Limitations**\n",
        "- May not cover specialized objects\n",
        "- Trained on general scenes (not always roads)\n",
        "- Accuracy depends on domain similarity\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    subgraph Pretraining[\"Pretraining (Done by YOLO team)\"]\n",
        "        A[COCO Dataset\\n330K images, 80 classes] --> B[Train YOLO\\non server GPUs]\n",
        "        B --> C[Pretrained Weights\\nyolov8n.pt]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "    subgraph Inference[\"Inference (Our Workshop)\"]\n",
        "        D[Our Road Image] --> C\n",
        "        C --> E[Detected Objects]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "\n",
        "    style Pretraining fill:#1a1a2e,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Inference fill:#2d3436,color:#fff\n",
        "    style C fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# YOLO Practical Pipeline {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### What You Will Do in the Notebook\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    S1[1. Install\\nultralytics] --> S2[2. Import\\nYOLO + cv2]\n",
        "    S2 --> S3[3. Download\\nroad image]\n",
        "    S3 --> S4[4. Load\\nmodel]\n",
        "    S4 --> S5[5. Run\\ninference]\n",
        "    S5 --> S6[6. Visualize\\nboxes]\n",
        "    S6 --> S7[7. Convert\\nto table]\n",
        "    S7 --> S8[8. Filter\\nroad objects]\n",
        "    S8 --> S9[9. Count\\nobjects]\n",
        "\n",
        "    style S5 fill:#f2994a,color:#fff\n",
        "    style S6 fill:#2f80ed,color:#fff\n",
        "    style S9 fill:#219653,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "Notebook file: `yolo_object_detection_workshop.ipynb` — each step above is a separate cell.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Objects We Care About {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### Road-Relevant Classes for an Intelligent Vehicle\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "| Class | Relevance |\n",
        "|:---|:---|\n",
        "| 🚶 **Person** | Safety-critical |\n",
        "| 🚗 **Car** | Most common on road |\n",
        "| 🏍️ **Motorcycle** | Common in Indonesia |\n",
        "| 🚌 **Bus** | Large vehicle, different behavior |\n",
        "| 🚛 **Truck** | Heavy vehicle, long braking |\n",
        "| 🚦 **Traffic Light** | Signal compliance |\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "### Why Filter?\n",
        "\n",
        "YOLO detects 80 classes out of the box — but we only need these 6 for driving.\n",
        "\n",
        "Classes we **ignore**:\n",
        "- 🍕 Pizza, 🛋️ Couch, 🧸 Teddy bear...\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "Notebook filters: `road_classes = [\"person\", \"car\", \"motorcycle\", \"bus\", \"truck\", \"traffic light\"]`\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"font-size: 0.8em; color: #888;\">\n",
        "In production, filtering by relevant classes reduces noise and improves safety.\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# From Detection to Decision {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### YOLO Detects Objects — But Who Makes the Decision?\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "### Detection Output\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "🚶 person × 3  (confidence: 0.9)\n",
        "🚗 car × 2     (confidence: 0.85)\n",
        "🚦 light × 1   (confidence: 0.78)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"4%\" style=\"font-size: 2em; padding-top: 30px; text-align: center;\"}>\n",
        "→\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "### Possible Decisions\n",
        "\n",
        "- 🛑 **Person ahead** → reduce speed, increase caution\n",
        "- 🚗 **Cars nearby** → maintain safe distance\n",
        "- 🚦 **Red light** → prepare to stop\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "**YOLO does NOT drive the vehicle.**  \n",
        "It provides perception. A separate planning/control module uses detection output alongside radar, LiDAR, maps, and rules to make decisions.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Practical Notebook Challenges {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "### What to Try After Completing the Walkthrough\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "### Part 1: Battery SoC\n",
        "\n",
        "- ✅ Complete the Linear Regression challenge (fill in the blanks)\n",
        "- ✅ Experiment with the Genetic Algorithm (cell 44-47)\n",
        "- ✅ Change RF/XGBoost hyperparameters manually\n",
        "- ✅ Plot prediction vs ground truth at different time windows\n",
        "- ✅ Discuss: why is R² below 0.5? What other features might help?\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n",
        "### Part 2: YOLOv8\n",
        "\n",
        "- ✅ Upload your own road image\n",
        "- ✅ Adjust confidence threshold (0.10 vs 0.60)\n",
        "- ✅ Count only vehicle classes (no pedestrians)\n",
        "- ✅ Compare crowded vs empty road scene\n",
        "- ✅ Write one driving decision based on the detection output\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Big Picture: Intelligent Vehicle System {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    subgraph Sensors[\"🔌 Sensors\"]\n",
        "        BMS[Battery Sensors\\nCurrent, Voltage, Temp]\n",
        "        CAM[Camera\\nRoad Scene]\n",
        "        RADAR[Radar\\nDistance, Speed]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "\n",
        "    subgraph Perception[\"🔍 ML Perception\"]\n",
        "        SOC[SoC Estimator\\nRandom Forest / XGBoost]\n",
        "        DET[Object Detector\\nYOLOv8]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "\n",
        "    subgraph Planning[\"🧠 Planning & Control\"]\n",
        "        ENERGY[Energy Manager]\n",
        "        PATH[Path Planner]\n",
        "        SAFETY[Safety Monitor]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "\n",
        "    subgraph Action[\"🎮 Vehicle Actions\"]\n",
        "        THR[Throttle / Brake Control]\n",
        "        BATT[Battery Charge Strategy]\n",
        "        ALERT[Driver Alerts]\n",
        "    end\n",
        "\n",
        "    BMS --> SOC\n",
        "    CAM --> DET\n",
        "    RADAR --> PATH\n",
        "    SOC --> ENERGY\n",
        "    DET --> PATH\n",
        "    DET --> SAFETY\n",
        "    ENERGY --> BATT\n",
        "    ENERGY --> THR\n",
        "    PATH --> THR\n",
        "    SAFETY --> ALERT\n",
        "\n",
        "    style Sensors fill:#1a1a2e,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Perception fill:#2d3436,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Planning fill:#1a1a2e,color:#fff\n",
        "    style Action fill:#2d3436,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 0.75em; color: #888; margin-top: 10px;\">\n",
        "SoC estimation and object detection are two perception blocks that feed into a larger vehicle intelligence system.\n",
        "</div>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Closing Reflection {.smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Three Questions to Take Home\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "> **1. What data can I collect?**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "> **2. What should the model predict?**\n",
        "\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "> **3. What decision will use that prediction?**\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    Q1[What data\\ncan I collect?] --> Q2[What should\\nthe model predict?]\n",
